{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract bam to-ubam [-h] [--r1 R1] [--r2 R2] [--sample SAMPLE] [--library LIBRARY]\n                              [--platform {ILLUMINA,DNBSEQ,ELEMENT,ULTIMA,PACBIO,ONT,IONTORRENT,LS454,SOLID,CAPILLARY}]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --r1 R1               Read 1 FASTQ (instead of an aligned --input BAM/CRAM).\n  --r2 R2               Read 2 FASTQ for paired-end --r1.\n  --sample SAMPLE       Sample name (SM) for FASTQ input, or for a BAM/CRAM without @RG lines\n                        (default: the input file name).\n  --library LIBRARY     Library name (LB) for a new read group.\n  --platform {ILLUMINA,DNBSEQ,ELEMENT,ULTIMA,PACBIO,ONT,IONTORRENT,LS454,SOLID,CAPILLARY}\n                        Sequencing platform (PL) for a new read group (default: detected from the\n                        read names).\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract bam to-ubam --input sample.cram\n  wgsextract bam to-ubam --r1 sample_R1.fastq.gz --r2 sample_R2.fastq.gz --sample NA12878\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <input stem>_unaligned.bam: queryname-sorted unaligned reads.\n\nneeds:\n  samtools; depending on options and inputs, also: bcftools; hours on a 30x\n  genome.\n",
